======================================================================================================================
STEP E -- THE EQUIVALENCE-PRINCIPLE LEMMA: y = |grad Phi|/a0 is not a local scalar of the metric
======================================================================================================================

The adversarial control first.  A naive 'curvature is second derivatives, a potential is not' argument is
WRONG as stated: on a one-parameter solution family you CAN build the Newtonian acceleration out of local
invariants, and C6 did exactly that.  G_loc = (sqrt3/2) K^{3/2}/|grad K| returns m/r^2 on Schwarzschild
exactly, to all orders.  So the lemma has to be proved by breaking G_loc, not by dimensional analysis.

  [PASS] E1  adding a uniform field Phi -> Phi + g.x leaves the FULL Hessian d_i d_j Phi unchanged   (hence every curvature tensor, every invariant, and every local functional of the metric)
  [PASS] E1b every local invariant (here K = 8Q and its gradient) is uniform-field blind

  MOND's y = |grad Phi|/a0 changes under the same shift.  This is not a technicality: the change
  IS the external field effect, one of MOND's defining and most-tested signatures.
    [canonical] star at 1 pc alone: y = 0.0015 ;  with the Galaxy's g_ext: y = 2.2153   (ratio 1488.0x)
    [alt      ] star at 1 pc alone: y = 0.0012 ;  with the Galaxy's g_ext: y = 1.8388   (ratio 1488.0x)
  [PASS] E2  y = |grad Phi|/a0 DOES change under the uniform shift, on both footings   (so y is not a diff-invariant local scalar of the metric  == LEMMA 1)
  [PASS] E3  Riemann-normal-coordinate form of Lemma 1: g=eta, dg=0 at any point p   (every local scalar at p is a function of curvature at p; y is not, because y != 0 in the freely falling frame's own y = 0)
  [PASS] E4  G_loc is 0/0 in a pure uniform field (K = 0 and |grad K| = 0 identically)   (a region containing only a coherent external field has NO local curvature to build y from)
  [PASS] E5a CONTROL: G_loc reproduces |grad Phi| EXACTLY for a point mass   (max relative error 3.55e-15 over r in [0.5, 20])

  Plummer sphere, scale b = 1:
    r/b =  0.20   G_loc/|grad Phi| = 10.9881
    r/b =  0.50   G_loc/|grad Phi| = 2.3143
